# fixedbugs, defect 582, lane b19-pack, 2026-10-10.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header of the program's own opening `#pragma pack(push, 1)`
# and never popping it packed every record its unit declared after it, so
# `main`, whose unit reads the header, laid `pair.Pair` out with no padding
# and `pair`'s unit, which does not, with seven bytes of it: `p.b` printed
# `1513209474796486656`, `pair.second(p)` a number of the stack, at exit
# 0, under clang's two `-Wpragma-pack` warnings.
#
# FIX: after the groups' close the unit gives back every state a header can
# leave set (`emit/header_state.hero`), `#pragma pack()` the packing among
# them, and clang's words on a header's packing left changed are quiet in
# the header's region, since they no longer reach a line the compiler writes.

use fixedbugs582/pair

extern "fixedbugs-582-a-header-s-unclosed-pack-push-leaves-two-modules-one-record-layout.h"
    function llabs(x: i64) -> i64

function main()
    p = pair.make(llabs(-123456789))
    print(p.b, " ", pair.second(p), " ", pair.second(pair.Pair(a: 2, b: llabs(-987654321))))
    print(pair.area(pair.shape(llabs(-7))))
